WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.788
Find the road reference point on Yuruga Street in The Gap, Brisbane.

00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:07.862
The eight pink spokes point upwind. Each sector label shows the input terrain category and ultimate velocity pressure.

00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:12.936
Switch to net windward wall pressure. This comparison assumes a wall normal to each approach.

00:00:12.936 --> 00:00:17.087
For this example only, assign a topographic multiplier of 1.25 to the northeast sector. The engineer determines this input from the site.

00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:22.109
Rotate the north model face to 22.5 degrees true. WindLab uses the sector factors around each new face normal.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:29.310
For the north face, the northeast approach at 45 degrees governs. Net wall pressure is 1.469 kPa ultimate and 0.688 kPa service.
